# Bulk pitch data stays out of the repo: data/raw (cached Savant CSV) and
# data/pitches (parquet) are fully regenerable via `mlbpitch backfill`.
# data/meta is tracked only for its small per-season files (fitted baselines,
# manifest, schedule, bios, leaderboards, free agents). The multi-season derived
# products -- profiles, embeddings, comps, snapshots, time series; ~190 MB, one
# file at 95 MB -- are rebuilt by scripts/ and stay out.
data/*
!data/meta/
data/meta/*_2024_2026.parquet
data/meta/umap_*.parquet

# SLURM job scripts and logs (cluster-specific: account and interpreter paths)
scripts/*.sbatch
*.log

# SLURM job output from scripts/refresh.sbatch also lands in data/meta
data/meta/refresh-*.log

# Personal working notes, not published: session logs, agent instructions,
# editor workspace, figure-style references
context/
CLAUDE.md
mlb.code-workspace
figure_aesthetics/

# Built page: published to the Hugging Face Space, rebuilt by scripts/atlas_build.py
analysis/pitch_atlas.html

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# Tooling
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store

# benchmark row-level outputs (regenerable: scripts/umap_benchmark.py); the write-up, figures and tables are tracked
analysis/umap_benchmark/*.parquet
# atlas build state: how the cached layout was made (regenerated by every full build)
data/meta/atlas_layout_*.json
